<!-- ═══ COMPLIANCE DISCLOSURE ═══
     Restored after being dropped in the Eleventy migration. Copy comes
     from the real disclosure graphic, not paraphrased.

     Two openers, both [data-compliance-open]: the announcement bar and
     the footer's legal row. The open/close JS mirrors the mobile menu
     exactly (inert the background, trap focus, Escape, return focus).

     The display rule is scoped to :not([hidden]) on purpose. Setting
     `display` unconditionally on a [hidden]-toggled element outranks the
     UA stylesheet's [hidden]{display:none}, which turns this into a
     full-viewport click-catcher that silently eats every click on the
     page. That bug shipped here once already. -->
<div class="compliance-modal" id="compliance-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
     aria-labelledby="compliance-title" hidden>
  <div class="compliance-scrim" data-compliance-close></div>

  <div class="compliance-card">
    <div class="compliance-head">
      <p class="t-label">Texas Delta-8 and Delta-10 ban &middot; In effect July 31</p>
      <button class="iconbtn" type="button" id="compliance-close" aria-label="Close">
        <svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#i-close"/></svg>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="compliance-body">
      <h2 class="t-display t-md" id="compliance-title">Sherpa remains<br>100% Texas compliant.</h2>
      <p class="compliance-lead">We're not pulling a single product.</p>

      <div class="compliance-section">
        <h3>What changed</h3>
        <p>
          As of July 31, Delta 8, Delta 10, and similar THC isomers are Schedule I controlled
          substances in Texas. Products containing them are coming off shelves across the state.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="compliance-section">
        <h3>Why Sherpa isn't affected</h3>
        <p>
          Every Sherpa product is made with <b>hemp derived Delta 9 THC at or below 0.3% by dry
          weight</b>, the standard under both Texas and federal law. Every batch is third party lab
          tested and supported by a Certificate of Analysis verifying compliance. Nothing in our
          lineup contains Delta 8 or Delta 10, so nothing is being pulled. Compliance isn't a
          checkbox for us. It's the foundation of this brand.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="compliance-section">
        <h3>Where we stand</h3>
        <p>
          We're not fans of bans, and we won't pretend otherwise. Tested, labeled, 21+ hemp products
          deserve smart regulation, and we'll keep making that case. We track every bill, rule, and
          ruling that touches hemp, and we'll keep you posted as things move.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="compliance-foot">
        21+ only &middot; Hemp derived Delta-9 THC &middot; Under 0.3% THC by weight &middot; Please enjoy responsibly
      </p>

      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/learn/lab-results/">
        See the lab results <svg width="18" height="18" class="arw" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
